'''Basommatophora''' (bā-som-a̤-tof′ọ̄-rä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < Gr. βάσις, base, + ὄμμα(τ-), eye, + -φόρος, < φέρειν = E. ''bear''<sup>1</sup>.] A division of pulmonate gastropodous mollusks, including those which have the eyes at the base of the tentacles, as in the families ''Auriculidæ'', ''Limnæidæ'', etc.: opposed to ''Stylommatophora''. See cut under ''Limnæidæ''.
